## Task ID

```
{{ task_id }}
```

## Your job

You need to get task description and context of this task for development.
You HAVE TO understand when to stop (you don't need a lot information - only relevant).

Use {{ fetch_cmd }} <taskId> to get task info and capture the output.
Read the task carefully. If the description references subtasks or linked tasks that are needed to
understand scope or context, fetch them too using the same tool with their IDs.

## Output

Emit your final reply as four independent XML-tagged blocks. Order does not matter.

```
<task_url>
<main task url here>
</task_url>

<task_title>
<one-line human-readable title of the main task, plain text, max 120 chars, in russian>
</task_title>

<main_task_info>
<main task info as markdown>
</main_task_info>

<additional_info>
<short summary of related tasks as markdown>
</additional_info>
```

Rules:
- main task description is not changable (but you MUST delete empty markdown blocks)
- no links needed or linked task ids
- you need to do short summary of linked task (not main task) and ONLY
  important information
- `<task_title>` must be a single line, no markdown, no quotes, suitable for a chat
  notification — used as the first line in the MR notification message
- emit each tag exactly once, opening and closing
- do NOT write a literal closing tag (e.g. `</main_task_info>`) inside the
  contents of a block — the parser stops at the first match. If you must
  show an example tag in markdown, wrap it in a code-fence and avoid the
  exact closing form.
